--- !u!114 &1552757545190895822
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 2960292302226113283}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: c5236d538fb060b48834286d70f34fa6, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: PILAR.Context::PILAR.Context.ContextNode
  _entries:
  - key: Function
    value: Reads the serial number the payload carries. It happens after the laser
      has fired but does NOT verify the mark - the laser writes the LaserMark datum
      and this reads SerialNumber. FG_02 is what reads the mark back.
  - key: Signal
    value: The PLC enables the camera, waits for Ready, triggers, and reads ResultValid
      / ResultOK. The twin itself only echoes enable and trigger and hands over the
      datum it read; Ready, Busy and the verdict are synthesised in OC_SIM FB_Camera,
      which compares the datum read for key SerialNumber against the expected value
      set in the group Mapping action - 60, which is what Assembly Part 1 carries.
      A pallet with no part reads 0 and fails.
  - key: BitLayout
    value: 2 of 8 control bits and 4 of 8 status bits used. Control bit 0 = enable,
      bit 1 = trigger. Status bit 0 = Ready, bit 1 = Busy, bit 2 = ResultValid, bit
      3 = ResultOK. The remaining bits are unused and unmapped. ResultOK is meaningless
      unless ResultValid is set.
  _topologySegment: 
  _topologyParent: {fileID: 0}
